{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558643329,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407cc05001sLyWaZfzkFHwvi","sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","messageID":"msg_1d407c475001Xw62q3vq98vOa9","type":"tool","id":"call_00_i3y78ndoc920fcvd9k20o64f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml, lines 1-73\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SETUP UMBRELLA (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator giving a first-run overview of every doctor command and running the existing read-only setup checks once\n5: purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run seven read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n6: action: Print the doctor target list -> run the seven read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   route_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\"\n35:   sk_code_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs\"\n36:   sk_git_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\"\n37:   trigger_index_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs\"\n38:   runtime_mirror_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n39:   hop_history: \".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs\"\n40:   hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n41:   codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # INPUTS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: inputs:\n47:   target: \"The command takes no positional target and no flag. /doctor:setup alone runs it; anything else fails before this YAML loads.\"\n48: \n49: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n50: # EXECUTION\n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: execution:\n53:   steps:\n54:     - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml and print the doctor target list through the presentation contract. The presentation table owns the rows and their wording. It shows /doctor:ci as one row for its report target. That row names the scaffold and toggle routes. Each row carries the one-line description of what it checks.\"\n55:     - \"Leg sk-code: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:sk-code setup.\"\n56:     - \"Leg sk-git: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>, where <name> is the AI tool executing this command: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name. Exit 0 passes. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, not a failure: no check failed, but one is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, so the row names /doctor:git setup to show which. Exit 2 is a usage error or a crash and is ERROR. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:git setup.\"\n57:     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n58:     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n59:     - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n60:     - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n61:     - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n62:     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n63:     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n64:     - \"Orphan processes (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --summary and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n65:     - \"Run every leg even when an earlier one fails, then render the per-leg table, the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary and the troubleshooting table through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # OUTPUT\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: output: |\n71:   STATUS=OK when no leg fails: each leg passes, is skipped or is degraded. List each degraded leg with the command that shows why.\n72:   STATUS=FAIL when any leg fails; list each failing leg with its repair command.\n73:   STATUS=ERROR when a leg crashes or its output cannot be read; report the message and the accepted invocation (/doctor:setup).","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml, lines 1-73\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SETUP UMBRELLA (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator giving a first-run overview of every doctor command and running the existing read-only setup checks once\n5: purpose: List every doctor target with what it checks, run seven read-only legs, and name the runnable doctor command that repairs each failing leg\n6: action: Print the doctor target list -> run the seven read-only legs once -> render the per-leg verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single-step\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"Every leg runs in its check-only form. This route MUST NOT regenerate the trigger index, sync a runtime mirror, start the advisor daemon, install hooks or provision the tree. A failing leg prints the doctor command that repairs it; repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of this diagnostic.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   route_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\"\n35:   sk_code_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs\"\n36:   sk_git_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\"\n37:   trigger_index_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs\"\n38:   runtime_mirror_check: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"\n39:   hop_history: \".skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs\"\n40:   hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n41:   codex_approval_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # INPUTS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: inputs:\n47:   target: \"The command takes no positional target and no flag. /doctor:setup alone runs it; anything else fails before this YAML loads.\"\n48: \n49: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n50: # EXECUTION\n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: execution:\n53:   steps:\n54:     - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml and print the doctor target list through the presentation contract. The presentation table owns the rows and their wording. It shows /doctor:ci as one row for its report target. That row names the scaffold and toggle routes. Each row carries the one-line description of what it checks.\"\n55:     - \"Leg sk-code: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/sk-code-setup-check.cjs. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:sk-code setup.\"\n56:     - \"Leg sk-git: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs --tool=<name>, where <name> is the AI tool executing this command: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name. Exit 0 passes. Exit 3 is DEGRADED, not a failure: no check failed, but one is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED, so the row names /doctor:git setup to show which. Exit 2 is a usage error or a crash and is ERROR. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:git setup.\"\n57:     - \"Leg trigger-index: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/generate-trigger-index.mjs --check --json. Exit 0 passes. Exit 1 (stale documents) or 2 and higher (unreadable index) fails, with repair /doctor:speckit.\"\n58:     - \"Leg runtime-mirrors: run node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check. Exit 0 passes. Any other exit fails, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors.\"\n59:     - \"Leg advisor: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --timeout-ms 500 --warm-only. Exit 0 with data.freshness set to live is PASS. Exit 0 with any other freshness is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. Exit 75 with a staleDistWarning field in stderr JSON is FAIL, with repair npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build. Exit 75 without that field is SKIP because the daemon is not running. Any other exit is FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor rebuild. When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.\"\n60:     - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\n61:     - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n62:     - \"Last session hop (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1 and show its first output line under the result as the last session hop, plus its open notes line when it prints one. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n63:     - \"Claude context window (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/hooks/session-relaunch/bin/session-relaunch.cjs window and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n64:     - \"Orphan processes (informational, not a leg): run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --summary and show its line. Its exit and output never change the status.\"\n65:     - \"Run every leg even when an earlier one fails, then render the per-leg table, the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary and the troubleshooting table through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # OUTPUT\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: output: |\n71:   STATUS=OK when no leg fails: each leg passes, is skipped or is degraded. List each degraded leg with the command that shows why.\n72:   STATUS=FAIL when any leg fails; list each failing leg with its repair command.\n73:   STATUS=ERROR when a leg crashes or its output cannot be read; report the message and the accepted invocation (/doctor:setup)."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558643205,"end":1794558643329}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558643357,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407cc530018XMcbqOWnHKWaJ","sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","messageID":"msg_1d407c475001Xw62q3vq98vOa9","type":"tool","id":"call_01_e6x74pwmc9e18utsxyjisrdx","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 1-111\n1: # /doctor:setup Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:setup`: the argument failure, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates, and next-step text. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: Unknown argument: [argument]\n9: /doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.\n10: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"\n11: ```\n12: \n13: ## 2. Doctor Target List\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n41: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n42: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n43: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n44: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n45: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n46: \n47: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n48: \n49: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n50: \n51: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n52: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n53: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n54: \n55: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n56: |-----|----------------------|\n57: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n58: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n59: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n60: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n62: | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n63: | delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n64: \n65: ## 4. Result Templates\n66: \n67: ### Summary\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n71: Target: setup\n72: Status: [OK|FAIL|ERROR]\n73: Mutation class: read-only\n74: Evidence: [N] legs, [N] passed, [N] failed, [N] skipped, [N] degraded, [N] errors\n75: Recommendation: [the doctor command for each failing or degraded leg, or none]\n76: Last session hop: [the first line `session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1` printed, or no hop recorded yet]\n77: [open notes: N handoff notes not claimed yet, oldest <filename>; shown only when history printed it]\n78: [the line `session-relaunch.cjs window` printed: Claude context window: N tokens, or Claude context window: none configured with the two settings that supply one]\n79: [orphans: N, about M MB; list them with node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --reap]\n80: STATUS=[status]\n81: ```\n82: \n83: The last session hop line is informational. It shows when a session last handed over, kept, claimed or finished a handoff, and it never changes the status. The open notes line appears only while a handoff note is still open, so a hand-over nobody finished stays visible.\n84: The Claude context window line is informational and never changes the status. It shows the window the Claude relaunch nudge measures against. When no window is configured it names `autoCompactWindow` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, and the nudge stays off until one is set or a `[1m]` model runs.\n85: The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n86: \n87: ### Failure Summary\n88: \n89: ```text\n90: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n91: Target: setup\n92: Step: [leg]\n93: Error: [message]\n94: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n95: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ## 5. Troubleshooting Display\n99: \n100: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n101: |-----------|------------------|\n102: | A leg reports FAIL | Run the doctor command in that leg's Repair cell, then rerun `/doctor:setup` |\n103: | The advisor leg reports SKIP | Exit 75 has no `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. The advisor daemon is stopped because `--warm-only` does not start it |\n104: | The advisor leg reports FAIL for a stale build | Exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. Run `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` |\n105: | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n106: | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n107: | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n108: | The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n109: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n110: \n111: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt, lines 1-111\n1: # /doctor:setup Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:setup`: the argument failure, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates, and next-step text. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: Unknown argument: [argument]\n9: /doctor:setup takes no target and no flag. Run /doctor:setup on its own.\n10: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"\n11: ```\n12: \n13: ## 2. Doctor Target List\n14: \n15: Render this table first, before any leg runs.\n16: \n17: | Command | What it checks |\n18: |---------|----------------|\n19: | `/doctor:setup` | This overview: the doctor target list and the seven read-only setup legs |\n20: | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem, with the class and the reason on every line |\n21: | `/doctor:env list` | The documented environment switches and where each value comes from |\n22: | `/doctor:update` | Whether a newer spec-kit release is available (bare runs the read-only check) |\n23: | `/doctor:git setup` | Whether the sk-git install, hooks, trust and standards are live |\n24: | `/doctor:git hooks` | Which shipped git hook gates are on or off, and switching one |\n25: | `/doctor:git standards` | The commit, PR and branch rules in .sk-git/ |\n26: | `/doctor:sk-code setup` | The sk-code setup battery, with a repair command per failing leg |\n27: | `/doctor:sk-code quality` | The repository quality config the gate reads with its tools, errors and disabled hygiene rules, then creating `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once |\n28: | `/doctor:ci report` | Lists every workflow with its switch state, trigger, filters and drift flags, read against the repository CI profile; `scaffold` and `toggle` are the confirmed action routes |\n29: | `/doctor:sk-skill check [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>]` | How far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format, row by row, with the repair for each finding |\n30: | `/doctor:sk-skill convert <name-or-path> [--dry-run]` | Moving one skill to the Skilled format: the plan, one yes per write, the backup, the write and the engine's undo block |\n31: | `/doctor:agents-md [check|embed|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run]` | The root instruction file: which shipped sections are current, embedding the template over a printed plan and its digest, and putting one recorded run back |\n32: | `/doctor:speckit` | The generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n33: | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Whether each runtime's agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors match .skilled |\n34: | `/doctor:skill-advisor tune` | Advisor recommendation quality and scoring tuning |\n35: | `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` | Rebuilding the skill graph database |\n36: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-budget` | Skill description character budgets |\n37: | `/doctor:skill-advisor parent-skill` | A parent skill hub's structure and registry |\n38: | `/doctor:skill-advisor skill-graph-freshness` | Drift between the compiled, SQLite and on-disk skill graph |\n39: | `/doctor:skill-advisor router-reach` | Whether each declared routing phrase reaches its hub |\n40: | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | Meaning matching for commands: whether the local embedder answers, what it costs, and the plan that pulls the model and starts the server after a yes |\n41: | `/doctor:deep-loop` | Deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n42: | `/doctor:mcp` | Code Mode install and debug, its UTCP configuration and runtime registration |\n43: | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Putting Skilled into your own project repo: the build check, what is already linked, and the ordered setup commands to run |\n44: | `/doctor:symlink [check|link|unlink] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | The framework links in a project repo: which runtime folders are linked, broken or missing, linking them over a printed plan and its digest, and undoing one recorded run |\n45: | `/doctor:overlay [status|apply|repin] [--json] [--root <dir>]` | A vendored Skilled tree's own overlays: which destinations are out of sync and why, then putting them back, capturing one live edit, or re-pinning the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan, after one yes |\n46: \n47: ## 3. Per-Leg Result Table\n48: \n49: Render one row per leg, in the workflow's order.\n50: \n51: | Leg | Command | Result | Repair |\n52: |-----|---------|--------|--------|\n53: | [leg] | [check-only command] | [PASS|FAIL|SKIP|DEGRADED|ERROR] | [the doctor command that repairs it or shows why, or none] |\n54: \n55: | Leg | Repair when it fails |\n56: |-----|----------------------|\n57: | sk-code | `/doctor:sk-code setup` |\n58: | sk-git | `/doctor:git setup` |\n59: | trigger-index | `/doctor:speckit` |\n60: | runtime-mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n61: | advisor | Stale build: `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`. Other FAIL or DEGRADED results: `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. |\n62: | embedder | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` |\n63: | delivery | Missing hook: /doctor:runtime-mirrors, or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. Unapproved Codex hook: the repair line the check prints, which opens /hooks in a Codex session |\n64: \n65: ## 4. Result Templates\n66: \n67: ### Summary\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n71: Target: setup\n72: Status: [OK|FAIL|ERROR]\n73: Mutation class: read-only\n74: Evidence: [N] legs, [N] passed, [N] failed, [N] skipped, [N] degraded, [N] errors\n75: Recommendation: [the doctor command for each failing or degraded leg, or none]\n76: Last session hop: [the first line `session-relaunch.cjs history --last 1` printed, or no hop recorded yet]\n77: [open notes: N handoff notes not claimed yet, oldest <filename>; shown only when history printed it]\n78: [the line `session-relaunch.cjs window` printed: Claude context window: N tokens, or Claude context window: none configured with the two settings that supply one]\n79: [orphans: N, about M MB; list them with node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/orphan-process-check.cjs --reap]\n80: STATUS=[status]\n81: ```\n82: \n83: The last session hop line is informational. It shows when a session last handed over, kept, claimed or finished a handoff, and it never changes the status. The open notes line appears only while a handoff note is still open, so a hand-over nobody finished stays visible.\n84: The Claude context window line is informational and never changes the status. It shows the window the Claude relaunch nudge measures against. When no window is configured it names `autoCompactWindow` and `SESSION_RELAUNCH_WINDOW_TOKENS`, and the nudge stays off until one is set or a `[1m]` model runs.\n85: The orphan line is informational only and never changes the doctor status. A model server kept on purpose with `SPECKIT_HF_MODEL_SERVER_ORPHAN_REAP=0` also shows as unsupervised, so do not reap it. With no orphan processes, print `orphans: none`. Run the listed `--reap` command to see each process, then use its confirmation command with `--yes` only when those are the processes to stop.\n86: \n87: ### Failure Summary\n88: \n89: ```text\n90: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n91: Target: setup\n92: Step: [leg]\n93: Error: [message]\n94: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n95: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ## 5. Troubleshooting Display\n99: \n100: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n101: |-----------|------------------|\n102: | A leg reports FAIL | Run the doctor command in that leg's Repair cell, then rerun `/doctor:setup` |\n103: | The advisor leg reports SKIP | Exit 75 has no `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. The advisor daemon is stopped because `--warm-only` does not start it |\n104: | The advisor leg reports FAIL for a stale build | Exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON. Run `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build` |\n105: | The advisor leg reports DEGRADED | Exit 0 has `data.freshness` other than `live`. The skill graph is not live. Run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n106: | The sk-git leg reports DEGRADED | No sk-git check failed, but one is unknown or a gate is saved off. Run `/doctor:git setup` to see which. On a runtime the battery cannot name, the AI-tool check stays unknown |\n107: | The trigger-index leg reports stale documents | Run `/doctor:speckit` to see which documents are stale |\n108: | The delivery leg reports DEGRADED | A runtime cannot receive the advisor brief. Run the repair the leg names, then rerun /doctor:setup. The install still works without it |\n109: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n110: \n111: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558643283,"end":1794558643357}}}}
