{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558647119,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407daeb001PXc0nCSEGtYJRN","sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","messageID":"msg_1d407d33d001pQWFUVGsV2qVP2","type":"tool","id":"call_00_67u0t43w6bpdw4xdfr9cli9b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 1-81\n1: ---\n2: description: \"List every doctor target and run the read-only setup checks, naming the repair command for each failing leg.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob\n5: ---\n6: <!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n7: \n8: # /doctor:setup Router\n9: \n10: This command is a thin, read-only router. It lists every doctor command and target with what each checks, runs the existing read-only checks once, and prints the runnable repair command for each failing leg. It writes nothing in the repository.\n11: \n12: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n13: \n14: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n15: \n16: Load the presentation contract before showing any dashboard, result summary, or next-step text.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n25: | Workflow | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n26: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest. This command owns the route whose `command` is `/doctor:setup`.\n33: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n34: - The command takes no positional target and no flag, so `/doctor:setup` alone runs it.\n35: - Any positional or flag fails before YAML load with the presentation contract's argument error.\n36: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n37: - The YAML owns workflow behavior. The presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n42: \n43: | Target | Workflow |\n44: |--------|----------|\n45: | `setup` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n46: \n47: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n48: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and select the `/doctor:setup` route.\n49: 3. Load `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` and execute it step by step.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n54: \n55: The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates and next-step text live only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n69: It shows an open-notes line while any handoff note is still unclaimed.\n70: It shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\n71: It shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\n72: That line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\n73: These lines are informational and never change the status.\n74: It writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\n75: The only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\n76: The default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\n77: The advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\n78: It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n79: It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n80: It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n81: It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md, lines 1-81\n1: ---\n2: description: \"List every doctor target and run the read-only setup checks, naming the repair command for each failing leg.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob\n5: ---\n6: <!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n7: \n8: # /doctor:setup Router\n9: \n10: This command is a thin, read-only router. It lists every doctor command and target with what each checks, runs the existing read-only checks once, and prints the runnable repair command for each failing leg. It writes nothing in the repository.\n11: \n12: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n13: \n14: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n15: \n16: Load the presentation contract before showing any dashboard, result summary, or next-step text.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n25: | Workflow | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n26: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest. This command owns the route whose `command` is `/doctor:setup`.\n33: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n34: - The command takes no positional target and no flag, so `/doctor:setup` alone runs it.\n35: - Any positional or flag fails before YAML load with the presentation contract's argument error.\n36: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n37: - The YAML owns workflow behavior. The presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n42: \n43: | Target | Workflow |\n44: |--------|----------|\n45: | `setup` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` |\n46: \n47: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n48: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and select the `/doctor:setup` route.\n49: 3. Load `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` and execute it step by step.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n54: \n55: The argument failure wording, the doctor target list, the per-leg result table, result templates and next-step text live only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n60: \n61: The workflow prints the doctor target list.\n62: It then runs seven read-only legs once: the sk-code setup battery, the sk-git setup battery, the trigger index freshness check, the runtime mirror check, the advisor status probe with `--warm-only` and the embedder check, which reads the semantic lane and the command vectors, and the delivery check, which reads whether each runtime's prompt hook is wired and whether Codex has approved it.\n63: The delivery leg reports DEGRADED, never FAIL, when a prompt hook is missing or the Codex hook is unapproved, and names the repair.\n64: It reports each leg as passing, skipped, degraded or failing.\n65: For a failing leg, it names the runnable doctor command that repairs it.\n66: The sk-git leg passes `--tool=<name>` for the AI tool running the command.\n67: Its exit 3 (an unknown check or a gate saved off) is degraded, not failing.\n68: After the legs, it shows the last session hop from the session-relaunch hop history.\n69: It shows an open-notes line while any handoff note is still unclaimed.\n70: It shows the Claude context window the relaunch nudge measures against, or the two settings that supply one when none is configured.\n71: It shows an orphans line from `orphan-process-check.cjs --summary`.\n72: That line counts leftover helper processes and model servers whose launcher died.\n73: These lines are informational and never change the status.\n74: It writes nothing in the repository and never starts the advisor daemon.\n75: The only write outside the repository is the advisor CLI creating its socket directory when that directory is absent.\n76: The default socket directory is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`.\n77: The advisor leg reports PASS when exit 0 has `data.freshness` set to `live`.\n78: It reports DEGRADED when exit 0 has any other freshness value and names `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n79: It reports FAIL when exit 75 includes `staleDistWarning` in stderr JSON and names `npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build`.\n80: It reports SKIP when exit 75 lacks that field because the daemon is stopped.\n81: It reports FAIL for any other exit with `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558647019,"end":1794558647119}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558647123,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407db3c0016c3v8SKAYPh8mN","sessionID":"ses_e2bf942faffeDhW8tELDRQaLaG","messageID":"msg_1d407d33d001pQWFUVGsV2qVP2","type":"tool","id":"call_01_hbfnyintbpxpf1m3b5dyzygm","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml, lines 1-69\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SYMLINK CHECK (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting the link state of one target repository against the Skilled manifest\n5: purpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\n6: action: Run the check engine once -> render its report through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single_step_check\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state. The route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, which reads each installed runtime's prompt hook entry and never writes.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n35:   manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n36:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n37:   hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # INPUTS\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: inputs:\n43:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n44:   root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n45:   runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:   include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:   link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:   json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n49:   target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # EXECUTION\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: execution:\n55:   steps:\n56:     - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n57:     - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n58:     - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n59:     - \"Exit 0 means no drift was found. Exit 1 means drift was found: broken links, foreign links, broken links inside merged folders, a missing source, or tracked absolute links. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Show the report and end with STATUS=WARN. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n60:     - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n61:     - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n68:   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n69:   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml, lines 1-69\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SYMLINK CHECK (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Diagnostic Operator reporting the link state of one target repository against the Skilled manifest\n5: purpose: Report the status of the core link, selected runtimes and extras by running the check engine once, then render its report through the presentation contract\n6: action: Run the check engine once -> render its report through the presentation contract\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: single_step_check\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: read_only\n16:   approvals: none\n17:   tracking: single_run\n18:   validation: read_only_assertion\n19: \n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state. The route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, which reads each installed runtime's prompt hook entry and never writes.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n35:   manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n36:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n37:   hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # INPUTS\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: inputs:\n43:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n44:   root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n45:   runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:   include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:   link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:   json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n49:   target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # EXECUTION\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: execution:\n55:   steps:\n56:     - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n57:     - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n58:     - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n59:     - \"Exit 0 means no drift was found. Exit 1 means drift was found: broken links, foreign links, broken links inside merged folders, a missing source, or tracked absolute links. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Show the report and end with STATUS=WARN. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n60:     - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n61:     - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n68:   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n69:   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558647101,"end":1794558647123}}}}
